  message: "ADR-0051 annotation (WI-virav; annotate only -- no fold, no closure, no re-prioritisation). CLAUSE VIOLATED (by the naive fix this item forbids): owner path \"spelled in the source language's import vocabulary\". NOTION: type, but package-STRIPPED (`Client`, not `net/http.Client`). A bare type is not an owner path, it is a name that collides -- which is exactly why carrying initializer types into the slot naively hijacks resolution at the measured 17.1%. The axiom says the fix is the QUALIFIED spelling (WI-vutav's constructor-qualifier fix is one instance), not more inference."  # 6301
